  "scope": [
    "Strict typed disposition prefix decoding preserves actual durable normalization/retirement intent-observation pairs, original private root identities, pending-last decision, partial attempts and exact canonical epochs. Decoded descriptions grant no ownership.",
    "Actual same-pool raw G0/G1 owners plus real canonical producer observations can create a separately registered read-only terminal observer. It creates no canonical writer lease, missing native marker, journal event or control publication, and cannot enroll a writer.",
    "Actual raw plan histories, observer/catalogue/field references and nested canonical facts remain independently sealed across finite prepaid non-reentrant native checks and full final teardown.",
    "Later disposition roots follow original quarantine, preserving all original data/inverse area indices and private inode/byte custody.",
    "A genuine separate OS process starts with empty registries, receives descriptive inputs only and reacquires actual raw owners to observe the completed disposition without recreating public native controls.",
    "Actual interruption after first exclusive native retirement observation ends all owners; a fresh canonical owner publishes a real missing G2 generation, a separately acknowledged disposition completes, and three-generation terminal replay preserves all previously retired private nodes.",
    "Distinct old owners may hand off the same incoming coordinate. Duplicate old group/path or raw identity/path and inconsistent per-epoch identity/group mappings refuse. Historical opaque IDs are not compared with freshly acquired plan identities; actual private-descriptor lineage remains the ownership proof."
  ],
